From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Nintendo DS build

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with the toolchain of the ports
(clang, calico and libnds), without SDL and the Apogee Sound System,
whose DS versions are in nds/. The engine is ARM code, its drawers run
from ITCM, the game is Thumb code, the parts that don't run every frame
optimized for size. The warnings about the old code mixing pointers and
integers and redefining libnds' types are left out. The DS has no
sys/uio.h, its picolibc has strlwr, strupr and itoa and only defines the
byte order in sys/types.h.
